			"notes": "## _RAINBOW_ Version 3\n\n![RAINBOW III!!! Java mod screenshot](https://github.com/jasonjgardner/minecraft-rtx-rainbow/assets/1903667/f2cbc153-752a-4181-8870-54ccc6aed60e)\n\n### New Color Palette\n- Version 3 no longer uses the Material Design color palette.\n- The palette has been reduced to match Minecraft's dye color variations. Includes shades 50-900.\n\n### New Materials\n- Each color is available in glossy, metallic, glass, and glowing varieties.\n- New blocks in a range of texture sizes. 16x, 32x, 64x, 128x and 256x.\n- Now includes stairs, slabs, carpets and mini cube models.*\n\n### Separated Functions\n- Removed functions for trails, structures, etc. from the base pack.\n- Scripts and functions will be available as another add-on.\n- Stargazer structures have been removed but can be easily recreated using [img2mcstructure](https://github.com/jasonjgardner/img2mcstructure).\n\n### Available for Java and Bedrock\n- RAINBOW III!!! is available as a Java mod and Bedrock add-on.\n- Bedrock add-on works with RTX and deferred rendering pipeline.\n- Java mods works with labPBR shaders.\n- Java mods require Minecraft __v1.20.1__ with __Forge__\n\n> *Models are currently only available in the Bedrock version.\n\n## Changelog\n* v2 stash by @jasonjgardner in https://github.com/jasonjgardner/minecraft-rtx-rainbow/pull/8\n* RAINBOW III!!! by @jasonjgardner in https://github.com/jasonjgardner/minecraft-rtx-rainbow/pull/9\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/jasonjgardner/minecraft-rtx-rainbow/compare/2.3.1...v3.0.0"
		}
